    "estimating time…": {},
    "flaccy · Recap": {},
    "flaccy, your lossless library": {},
    "iOS mixes all audio — your music plus system sounds — into one stream and re-encodes it to AAC for Bluetooth, so even a 256 kbps AAC file is decoded and encoded again on its way to your AirPods. This is how the audio pipeline works: engineering consensus, as Apple doesn't document passthrough. One extra generation of high-bitrate AAC is essentially inaudible — the loss is real on paper, tiny in practice.": {},
